cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "prooflock: configuration-independent verification of a machine-protection interlock chain (JET case study) in Bend 2"
abstract: >-
  A verified reference model of the JET wall-protection chain (JTT / RTPS / PTN / DMS)
  written in Bend 2: laws over every urgency order, control state, event and counter value,
  decided by a finite certificate and lifted to universal theorems by reflection, with
  soundness lemmas for the specification predicates, a Python re-execution of the certificate
  (another language, not an independent implementation), an adversarial mutation bank on the
  Python reference model (76 defects: 75 killed by the laws re-encoded in Python and a check that
  the model's invariant is the specification's; the survivor computed equivalent by the gate)
  judged against specification constants,
  and differential testing of a production implementation. The specifications, models, laws and
  proofs were written by an AI system (Claude, Anthropic) directed and audited by a human author;
  the adversarial reviews recorded in the docs are automated passes, not independent human evaluation.
authors:
  - family-names: "Colombo Barceló"
    given-names: "Franco"
license: Apache-2.0
